From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:33:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Athena API: players move between worlds on different threads

Document the two-step move, logins aimed at a world on its own thread, and that
teleportAsync runs and completes on the thread of the entity's world.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
index c950fa77f8584a9bee9049541a03ce11c65a9b0c..f2a0f393c6d5ced7e34975eaed67c663b2d43d79 100644
--- a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
+++ b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
@@ -222,12 +222,13 @@ public final class Athena {
     /**
      * Teleports {@code entity} once the chunk at {@code location} is loaded, loading it off the
      * server thread first if it is not - Paper's {@code Entity#teleportAsync}. The teleport itself
-     * happens on the server thread; what is asynchronous is the chunk read. It does not make the
-     * work after the teleport any lighter: for many players at once, see
-     * {@link #teleportGradually(List, List, int)}.
+     * happens on the thread that ticks the entity's world (the server thread unless the world has
+     * its own, see {@link #startWorldThread}); what is asynchronous is the chunk read. May be called
+     * from any thread. It does not make the work after the teleport any lighter: for many players at
+     * once, see {@link #teleportGradually(List, List, int)}.
      *
-     * @return completes on the server thread: true if the entity was teleported, false if it was
-     *         gone by then or a plugin cancelled the teleport
+     * @return completes on the thread that ticks the entity's world: true if the entity was
+     *         teleported, false if it was gone by then or a plugin cancelled the teleport
      */
     public static CompletableFuture<Boolean> teleportAsync(Entity entity, Location location) {
         return getServer().teleportAsync(entity, location);
@@ -413,9 +414,12 @@ public final class Athena {
      * use {@link #runOnWorld} to work on it from elsewhere. Aikar's timings are turned off.
      *
      * <p>Players in the world go with it: their packets, connection ticks, commands, chat
-     * callbacks and quits run on the world's thread. Not yet: players and entities cannot change
-     * worlds into or out of it (teleports are refused, a respawn stays in the world, a login never
-     * lands in it), {@link #preloadChunks} refuses it, and the main world cannot have its own thread.
+     * callbacks and quits run on the world's thread. A player moves between worlds ticked by
+     * different threads in two steps: it leaves on its old world's thread and arrives on the new
+     * one's, so {@code teleport} returns before the player is there, and a player on the way cannot
+     * be teleported again. A login aimed at such a world lands in the main world and is then moved.
+     * Entities other than players do not move between worlds ticked by different threads, and the
+     * main world cannot have its own thread.
      *
      * @throws IllegalStateException if {@code world} is the main world, or this is called from inside
      *         the world's own tick
